  {
   "label": {
    "none": [
     "ai-summary"
    ]
   },
   "value": {
    "none": [
     "In the letter, Lieut J. H. Massey informs his wife, Barbara, about his continued deployment to the Middle East. He mentions uncertainty about when they might be sent off, possibly within two to five days. Massey expresses his sadness at leaving Barbara and leaves the decision to her regarding whether she should visit him before he departs. The letter is signed \\Always your Harry\\ and includes a postmark dated September 14, 1940."
    ]
   }
